 Accessibility Compliance\n\nNuevo archivo:\n- backend/services/accessibilityAuditor.js (850+ líneas)\n  * HTML auditing con cheerio parsing\n  * 7 categorías de auditoría WCAG 2.1 Level AA\n  * Auto-fix para issues comunes\n  * Scoring y compliance reporting\n\nFeatures implementadas:\n✅ ARIA Labels and Roles (WCAG 4.1.2)\n  - Detecta buttons/links sin accessible name\n  - Valida inputs sin labels\n  - Verifica ARIA roles válidos\n\n✅ Image Alt Text (WCAG 1.1.1)\n  - Detecta imágenes sin alt attribute\n  - Identifica alt text con filenames\n  - Sugiere alt=\"\" para decorativas\n\n✅ Form Labels (WCAG 3.3.2)\n  - Verifica labels para inputs/select/textarea\n  - Detecta placeholder usado como label (bad practice)\n  - Valida aria-required en required fields\n\n✅ Heading Structure (WCAG 1.3.1)\n  - Detecta múltiples h1 (should be one per page)\n  - Identifica heading level skipping (h2 → h4)\n  - Verifica headings no vacíos\n\n✅ Link Text (WCAG 2.4.4)\n  - Detecta generic link text (\"click here\", \"read more\")\n  - Verifica links con accessible name\n  - Sugiere descriptive text\n\n✅ Keyboard Navigation (WCAG 2.1.1)\n  - Detecta positive tabindex values (bad practice)\n  - Verifica onclick sin keyboard handlers\n  - Sugiere usar <button> en lugar de div/span clickable\n\n✅ Semantic HTML (WCAG 1.3.1)\n  - Detecta div/span con onclick (should be button)\n  - Verifica landmarks (<main>, <nav>)\n  - Sugiere semantic elements\n\nAuto-fix capabilities:\n✅ Add empty alt to decorative images\n✅ Add aria-required to required inputs\n✅ Add role=\"button\" + tabindex=\"0\" to clickable divs/spans\n✅ Remove positive tabindex values (replace with 0)\n\nAudit report structure:\n{\n  totalIssues: 45,\n  issues: [{ category, severity, wcagCriterion, element, message, html, fix }],\n  byCategory: { ARIA: [...], Forms: [...], ... },\n  compliance: { score: 78, grade: ''C'' },\n  wcagLevel: ''Partially Compliant''\n}\n\nDependencias:\n- cheerio: HTML parsing y manipulation (22 packages)\n\nUso:\nconst accessibilityAuditor = require(''./services/accessibilityAuditor'');\n\n// Audit HTML\nconst report = await accessibilityAuditor.auditHTML(htmlContent);\n\n// Auto-fix issues\nconst fixed = await accessibilityAuditor.autoFix(htmlContent);\n\nSeverity levels:\n- high: Critical accessibility barriers\n- medium: Significant issues affecting usability\n- low: Minor improvements\n\nTotal SEMANA 27-28 (parcial): ~2,120 líneas de código\nEstado: v5.3.0 → v5.3.5 (WCAG auditor completo)\n\nPróximo: SOC2 Readiness (audit logging, access controls, encryption)","tree":{"sha":"e15e07dd987e4ce6c702061178e8d0d6729c17db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SACRINT/sipweb-bg/git/trees/e15e07dd987e4ce6c702061178e8d0d6729c17db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SACRINT/sipweb-bg/git/commits/9e31da262b83afbc56a1c6a81a55a493d3e88649","verification":{"payload":"tree e15e07dd987e4ce6c702061178e8d0d6729c17db\nparent a2edf9ada6f1aea4c2dc625793ab7f60b3826d3c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1763671228 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1763671228 +0000\n\nfeat(semana-27): WCAG 2.1 AA Accessibility Auditor completo\n\nTAREA 2: WCAG 2.1 Level AA Accessibility Compliance\n\nNuevo archivo:\n- backend/services/accessibilityAuditor.js (850+ líneas)\n  * HTML auditing con cheerio parsing\n  * 7 categorías de auditoría WCAG 2.1 Level AA\n  * Auto-fix para issues comunes\n  * Scoring y compliance reporting\n\nFeatures implementadas:\n✅ ARIA Labels and Roles (WCAG 4.1.2)\n  - Detecta buttons/links sin accessible name\n  - Valida inputs sin labels\n  - Verifica ARIA roles válidos\n\n✅ Image Alt Text (WCAG 1.1.1)\n  - Detecta imágenes sin alt attribute\n  - Identifica alt text con filenames\n  - Sugiere alt=\"\" para decorativas\n\n✅ Form Labels (WCAG 3.3.2)\n  - Verifica labels para inputs/select/textarea\n  - Detecta placeholder usado como label (bad practice)\n  - Valida aria-required en required fields\n\n✅ Heading Structure (WCAG 1.3.1)\n  - Detecta múltiples h1 (should be one per page)\n  - Identifica heading level skipping (h2 → h4)\n  - Verifica headings no vacíos\n\n✅ Link Text (WCAG 2.4.4)\n  - Detecta generic link text (\"click here\", \"read more\")\n  - Verifica links con accessible name\n  - Sugiere descriptive text\n\n✅ Keyboard Navigation (WCAG 2.1.1)\n  - Detecta positive tabindex values (bad practice)\n  - Verifica onclick sin keyboard handlers\n  - Sugiere usar <button> en lugar de div/span clickable\n\n✅ Semantic HTML (WCAG 1.3.1)\n  - Detecta div/span con onclick (should be button)\n  - Verifica landmarks (<main>, <nav>)\n  - Sugiere semantic elements\n\nAuto-fix capabilities:\n✅ Add empty alt to decorative images\n✅ Add aria-required to required inputs\n✅ Add role=\"button\" + tabindex=\"0\" to clickable divs/spans\n✅ Remove positive tabindex values (replace with 0)\n\nAudit report structure:\n{\n  totalIssues: 45,\n  issues: [{ category, severity, wcagCriterion, element, message, html, fix }],\n  byCategory: { ARIA: [...], Forms: [...], ... },\n  compliance: { score: 78, grade: ''C'' },\n  wcagLevel: ''Partially Compliant''\n}\n\nDependencias:\n- cheerio: HTML parsing y manipulation (22 packages)\n\nUso:\nconst accessibilityAuditor = require(''./services/accessibilityAuditor'');\n\n// Audit HTML\nconst report = await accessibilityAuditor.auditHTML(htmlContent);\n\n// Auto-fix issues\nconst fixed = await accessibilityAuditor.autoFix(htmlContent);\n\nSeverity levels:\n- high: Critical accessibility barriers\n- medium: Significant issues affecting usability\n- low: Minor improvements\n\nTotal SEMANA 27-28 (parcial): ~2,120 líneas de código\nEstado: v5.3.0 → v5.3.5 (WCAG auditor completo)\n\nPróximo: SOC2 Readiness (audit logging, access controls, encryption)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNNWsyVP\neV+qIatuTWJ3EZFWYpcKqparalqro7