User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/b3fae66e3bc381d3ac01268dae807a8fc2cf2413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:25:15Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:25:15Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"render: add RenderOneText (text/template) render path\n\nRenderOne used html/template, which HTML-escapes every [[ ]] action''s\noutput. host-manager reuses RenderOne to render text-page bodies\n(robots.txt, llms.txt, etc.), so a value containing &, <, >, \" came\nout corrupted, and a structured body could trip an html/template\ncontext error at Execute.\n\nAdd RenderOneText, identical to RenderOne except it parses/executes\nwith text/template so action output is emitted verbatim. Factor the\nshared FuncMap construction (sprig + extract/l10n/number/currency/\npercent/bytes/date/pop/sortBy) out of RenderOne into a private\nfuncMap() helper used by both render paths, instead of duplicating it.\nhtml/template.FuncMap is a type alias for text/template.FuncMap, so\nthe same funcs value works unmodified with both engines'' .Funcs().\n\nRenderOne is otherwise unchanged: still html/template, same [[ ]]\ndelimiters, same signature — HTML pages keep their escaping.\n\nTDD: added TestRenderOneText_DoesNotEscapeHTMLSpecialChars (RED before\nRenderOneText existed) plus a contrasting TestRenderOne_EscapesHTMLSpecialChars,\nTestRenderOneText_InvalidTemplate, and TestRenderOneText_SharesFuncMap.\n\nmake test and make lint pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6926c1e4d8da34023a83f42499e8b6b15328cc3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/6926c1e4d8da34023a83f42499e8b6b15328cc3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/b3fae66e3bc381d3ac01268dae807a8fc2cf2413","verification":{"payload":"tree 6926c1e4d8da34023a83f42499e8b6b15328cc3c\nparent 720f2c5482e7a6b78ce91e2e8913039b13095b71\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1788402315 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1788402315 -0400\n\nrender: add RenderOneText (text/template) render path\n\nRenderOne used html/template, which HTML-escapes every [[ ]] action''s\noutput. host-manager reuses RenderOne to render text-page bodies\n(robots.txt, llms.txt, etc.), so a value containing &, <, >, \" came\nout corrupted, and a structured body could trip an html/template\ncontext error at Execute.\n\nAdd RenderOneText, identical to RenderOne except it parses/executes\nwith text/template so action output is emitted verbatim. Factor the\nshared FuncMap construction (sprig + extract/l10n/number/currency/\npercent/bytes/date/pop/sortBy) out of RenderOne into a private\nfuncMap() helper used by both render paths, instead of duplicating it.\nhtml/template.FuncMap is a type alias for text/template.FuncMap, so\nthe same funcs value works unmodified with both engines'' .Funcs().\n\nRenderOne is otherwise unchanged: still html/template, same [[ ]]\ndelimiters, same signature — HTML pages keep their escaping.\n\nTDD: added TestRenderOneText_DoesNotEscapeHTMLSpecialChars (RED before\nRenderOneText existed) plus a contrasting TestRenderOne_EscapesHTMLSpecialChars,\nTestRenderOneText_InvalidTemplate, and TestRenderOneText_SharesFuncMap.\n\nmake test and make lint pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCvpESyYR33/xeLHvNz08VrD6OaOLObTUGhWmziAu0qaDBnSzXi6+Uprus/X10Tq/+\nIKi6XDH2TGjyGzSMo9gAc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T02:29:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.