ollowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/720f2c5482e7a6b78ce91e2e8913039b13095b71","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKDcyMGYyYzU0ODJlN2E2Yjc4Y2U5MWUyZTg5MTMwMzliMTMwOTViNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34","sha":"d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34"}],"sha":"720f2c5482e7a6b78ce91e2e8913039b13095b71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/720f2c5482e7a6b78ce91e2e8913039b13095b71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:44:48Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:44:48Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"feat(api): KDexPage localized flag + text-serving (mimeType, body)\n\nAdds three optional KDexPageSpec fields so a KDexPage can serve a raw\ntext document instead of composing HTML from an archetype:\n\n- Localized *bool (default true): gates language-prefixed route\n  registration; false pins a page to exactly one path (robots.txt,\n  llms.txt, sitemap.xml).\n- MimeType string (enum txt/json/yaml/markdown/xml): when set, serves\n  Body as a raw text document of this type.\n- Body string (maxLength 65536): the content served when mimeType is\n  set, through the same [[ ]] template + translation pipeline as a\n  rawHTML content entry.\n\ncontentEntries is relaxed from Required/MinItems=1 to Optional (still\nMaxItems=32); the \"main slot\" guarantee moves to two spec-level CEL\nrules: mimeType and body must be set together, and an HTML page (no\nmimeType) must still declare a ''main'' contentEntries slot.\n\nDeviation from the task brief: protobuf field numbers are 14/15/16,\nnot 13/14/15 -- KDexPageSpec.Security already occupies 13 (added in\n80d3a22, before the brief was written). Verified by reading the\nstruct as instructed.\n\nmake generate regenerated zz_generated.deepcopy.go (DeepCopyInto for\nthe new *bool) and make manifests regenerated\nconfig/crd/bases/kdex.dev_kdexpages.yaml.\n\nThis repo has no envtest (confirmed: no envtest/apiserver dependency\nin go.mod, `make test` = manifests generate fmt vet + go test, no\ninternal/ controller package -- consistent with this repo''s own\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-24-kdexfunction-service-backend.md,\nwhich notes the same for a prior CEL-bearing change). So the new\nCEL rules'' admission -- including proving they stay within the\napiserver''s per-rule cost budget -- is not verified here; it is\nexercised by kdex-host-manager''s envtest suite in a later phase of\nthis plan. kdexpage_types_test.go adds a decode test for the new\nfields plus a generated-schema assertion test (mirroring\nTestKDexFunctionBasePathSchema) that checks the markers, enum,\nmaxLength, and both CEL rule strings landed in the generated CRD\nYAML unchanged -- the strongest signal available without envtest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"25ee8c6898f864da0a0cdde96b1a91233dda1ff9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/25ee8c6898f864da0a0cdde96b1a91233dda1ff9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34","verification":{"payload":"tree 25ee8c6898f864da0a0cdde96b1a91233dda1ff9\nparent 6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1788363888 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1788363888 -0400\n\nfeat(api): KDexPage localized flag + text-serving (mimeType, body)\n\nAdds three optional KDexPageSpec fields so a KDexPage can serve a raw\ntext document instead of composing HTML from an archetype:\n\n- Localized *bool (default true): gates language-prefixed route\n  registration; false pins a page to exactly one path (robots.txt,\n  llms.txt, sitemap.xml).\n- MimeType string (enum txt/json/yaml/markdown/xml): when set, serves\n  Body as a raw text document of this type.\n- Body string (maxLength 65536): the content served when mimeType is\n  set, through the same [[ ]] template + translation pipeline as a\n  rawHTML content entry.\n\ncontentEntries is relaxed from Required/MinItems=1 to Optional (still\nMaxItems=32); the \"main slot\" guarantee moves to two spec-level CEL\nrules: mimeType and body must be set together, and an HTML page (no\nmimeType) must still declare a ''main'' contentEntries slot.\n\nDeviation from the task brief: protobuf field numbers are 14/15/16,\nnot 13/14/15 -- KDexPageSpec.Security already occupies 13 (added in\n80d3a22, before the brief was written). Verified by reading the\nstruct as instructed.\n\nmake generate regenerated zz_generated.deepcopy.go (DeepCopyInto for\nthe new *bool) and make manifests regenerated\nconfig/crd/bases/kdex.dev_kdexpages.yaml.\n\nThis repo has no envtest (confirmed: no envtest/apiserver dependency\nin go.mod, `make test` = manifests generate fmt vet + go test, no\ninternal/ controller package -- consistent with this repo''s own\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-24-kdexfunction-service-backend.md,\nwhich notes the same for a prior CEL-bearing change). So the new\nCEL rules'' admission -- including proving they stay within the\napiserver''s per-rule cost budget -- is not verified here; it is\nexercised by kdex-host-manager''s envtest suite in a later phase of\nthis plan. kdexpage_types_test.go adds a decode test for the new\nfields plus a generated-schema assertion test (mirroring\nTestKDexFunctionBasePathSchema) that checks the markers, enum,\nmaxLength, and both CEL rule strings landed in the generated CRD\nYAML unchanged -- the strongest signal available without envtest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKfNMHZC+WsT5sevWs9yTFkUCsBYnIW6fUXcksw0pWesCwyL2QLznxHepUZUQjtt3z\nhiIi3GgV0YObyEkLCnxAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T16:17:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGQ0MmNlNzY0MDA4MDc2NGExNGZhODk5MzAzMGQxMjIxN2JiMThkMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9","sha":"6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9"}],"sha":"d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d42ce7640080764a14fa8993030d12217bb18d34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:10:34Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:10:34Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"fix(api): end-anchor and bound KDexFunction spec.api.basePath\n\nThe pattern was `^/\\w+/\\w+` — start-anchored only, no length bound — so\n`/a/b\",resource_metadata=\"https://attacker.example/x` was a valid basePath.\nkdex-host-manager interpolates this value into the RFC 9728 resource_metadata\nparameter of a WWW-Authenticate header, which is an HTTP quoted-string, so an\nauthor with KDexFunction rights could close the quote, inject a second\nresource_metadata parameter, and steer an RFC 9728 client to an attacker-run\nauthorization server. host-manager now drops an unsafe pointer at both\nemitters; this closes it at the producer so the value cannot be authored.\n\nNew rule: `^(/\\w[\\w-]*){2,8}$` with MaxLength=64.\n\nSimply appending `$` would have broken production twice over:\n\n  - Three-segment basePaths are the norm, not an edge case: all seven knowdb-*\n    functions use /api/v1/<name> on every cluster. `^/\\w+/\\w+$` rejects them.\n  - /v1/credential-check contains a hyphen, which \\w does not match. It passes\n    today only because the pattern is unanchored and /v1/credential matches as\n    a prefix. Any end-anchored pattern built from \\w alone rejects a CR that is\n    live in dev and prod.\n\nRequiring each segment to start with \\w (rather than allowing a bare [\\w-]+)\npreserves a property the old pattern had by accident: /-/openapi stays\nunauthorable, so a function cannot shadow the host''s reserved /-/ route prefix.\nMaxLength=64 gives ~3x headroom over the longest real value\n(/api/v1/vector_stores, 21) and newly bounds a field read by the sibling CEL\nrule, lowering the CRD''s estimated validation cost.\n\nThe Go-side basePathRegex/pathItemPathRegex are deliberately unchanged: they\nare consumed by host-manager''s sniffer against incoming *request* paths, where\nprefix anchoring is required for routing to work.\n\nVerified: CRD server-dry-run installs on a live 1.36 apiserver; the three CR\ncases dry-run against a real apiserver (envtest 1.35) accept the multi-segment,\nhyphenated and two-segment forms and reject the injection payload; all 18\ndistinct basePaths live across 6 clusters still validate.\n\nAdds a regression test that reads the generated CRD rather than the marker, so\na marker that stops taking fails `make test`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"435b27501e6169c771a30a226cb4eddfa6a816f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/435b27501e6169c771a30a226cb4eddfa6a816f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 435b27501e6169c771a30a226cb4eddfa6a816f5\nparent e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1788027034 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1788027034 -0400\n\nfix(api): end-anchor and bound KDexFunction spec.api.basePath\n\nThe pattern was `^/\\w+/\\w+` — start-anchored only, no length bound — so\n`/a/b\",resource_metadata=\"https://attacker.example/x` was a valid basePath.\nkdex-host-manager interpolates this value into the RFC 9728 resource_metadata\nparameter of a WWW-Authenticate header, which is an HTTP quoted-string, so an\nauthor with KDexFunction rights could close the quote, inject a second\nresource_metadata parameter, and steer an RFC 9728 client to an attacker-run\nauthorization server. host-manager now drops an unsafe pointer at both\nemitters; this closes it at the producer so the value cannot be authored.\n\nNew rule: `^(/\\w[\\w-]*){2,8}$` with MaxLength=64.\n\nSimply appending `$` would have broken production twice over:\n\n  - Three-segment basePaths are the norm, not an edge case: all seven knowdb-*\n    functions use /api/v1/<name> on every cluster. `^/\\w+/\\w+$` rejects them.\n  - /v1/credential-check contains a hyphen, which \\w does not match. It passes\n    today only because the pattern is unanchored and /v1/credential matches as\n    a prefix. Any end-anchored pattern built from \\w alone rejects a CR that is\n    live in dev and prod.\n\nRequiring each segment to start with \\w (rather than allowing a bare [\\w-]+)\npreserves a property the old pattern had by accident: /-/openapi stays\nunauthorable, so a function cannot shadow the host''s reserved /-/ route prefix.\nMaxLength=64 gives ~3x headroom over the longest real value\n(/api/v1/vector_stores, 21) and newly bounds a field read by the sibling CEL\nrule, lowering the CRD''s estimated validation cost.\n\nThe Go-side basePathRegex/pathItemPathRegex are deliberately unchanged: they\nare consumed by host-manager''s sniffer against incoming *request* paths, where\nprefix anchoring is required for routing to work.\n\nVerified: CRD server-dry-run installs on a live 1.36 apiserver; the three CR\ncases dry-run against a real apiserver (envtest 1.35) accept the multi-segment,\nhyphenated and two-segment forms and reject the injection payload; all 18\ndistinct basePaths live across 6 clusters still validate.\n\nAdds a regression test that reads the generated CRD rather than the marker, so\na marker that stops taking fails `make test`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOdNGO7bkY8KG6McpuHyOt8wt+JPUCgW/+82a7S0Sehd5yOIoHmeP0Z6pQlU//AukW\nGU18/cCnJuzH3UkioJ4wQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T04:36:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKDY5ODNkMmQ5NWQ2ZWFkYmIyYTdjZmU2MWIwNjRjZDJjMGMwZDAxZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca","sha":"e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca"}],"sha":"6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/6983d2d95d6eadbb2a7cfe61b064cd2c0c0d01e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:07:43Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:07:43Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"ci: install the same golangci-lint the Makefile pins\n\nThe previous commit moved GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION to v2.13.2 but CI does not\nread it: the workflow installs the linter through golangci-lint-action''s\nown `version:`, which was still v2.10.1. So CI kept using the version that\ncannot parse go1.27 export data AND rejected `linters.settings.goconst.\nignore-tests`, a key that version predates -- failing at `config verify`\nbefore a single file was linted.\n\nBoth pins now say v2.13.2 and each carries a comment pointing at the\nother, because one tool with two version declarations is exactly what let\nthis through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5cd12e796e70dfc8452ea22b61ae8753e2eed30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/b5cd12e796e70dfc8452ea22b61ae8753e2eed30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca","verification":{"payload":"tree b5cd12e796e70dfc8452ea22b61ae8753e2eed30\nparent e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787933263 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787933263 -0400\n\nci: install the same golangci-lint the Makefile pins\n\nThe previous commit moved GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION to v2.13.2 but CI does not\nread it: the workflow installs the linter through golangci-lint-action''s\nown `version:`, which was still v2.10.1. So CI kept using the version that\ncannot parse go1.27 export data AND rejected `linters.settings.goconst.\nignore-tests`, a key that version predates -- failing at `config verify`\nbefore a single file was linted.\n\nBoth pins now say v2.13.2 and each carries a comment pointing at the\nother, because one tool with two version declarations is exactly what let\nthis through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHbOJm7cWHNAzwnJbf6RSP4v+gNkiQEZzbRfQkwbvp9vXBbymblq/MJRaXIr7X53wG\nOL9XM2byCuqd4x+g6Xgg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T16:07:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGU2MjdhODk5ZWM3MjNlNjViNWU3M2RhMWE3MmM1ZTVmMTQwZjU0Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28","sha":"e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28"}],"sha":"e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/e627a899ec723e65b5e73da1a72c5e5f140f54ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:05:40Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:05:40Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"build(lint): upgrade golangci-lint to v2.13.2 and fix what it found\n\n`make lint` panicked on any tree, which also meant ./updateCrdUsage.sh -t\ncould not run its own gate: the pinned v2.10.1 is built by go-install-tool\nwith whatever Go is on PATH, and its vendored x/tools cannot decode go1.27\nexport data. Rebuilding the same version does not help, so the pin had to\nmove; v2.13.2 is current.\n\nThe upgrade reported 38 findings on a previously-clean tree. 36 were\ngoconst in _test.go files -- a table repeating a literal across twenty\ncases is the point of the table -- so goconst now ignores tests.\n\nThe two in real code are fixed rather than exempted: reflect.Ptr is the\ndeprecated spelling of reflect.Pointer, and render/validate.go''s sample\npage paths are now named, which is also what the fixture was demonstrating\n(the same path appears as both a BasePath and an Href within one entry).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df9cf7596d889e14475c80fd080cfcd0bfcb09f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/df9cf7596d889e14475c80fd080cfcd0bfcb09f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28","verification":{"payload":"tree df9cf7596d889e14475c80fd080cfcd0bfcb09f6\nparent 7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787933140 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787933140 -0400\n\nbuild(lint): upgrade golangci-lint to v2.13.2 and fix what it found\n\n`make lint` panicked on any tree, which also meant ./updateCrdUsage.sh -t\ncould not run its own gate: the pinned v2.10.1 is built by go-install-tool\nwith whatever Go is on PATH, and its vendored x/tools cannot decode go1.27\nexport data. Rebuilding the same version does not help, so the pin had to\nmove; v2.13.2 is current.\n\nThe upgrade reported 38 findings on a previously-clean tree. 36 were\ngoconst in _test.go files -- a table repeating a literal across twenty\ncases is the point of the table -- so goconst now ignores tests.\n\nThe two in real code are fixed rather than exempted: reflect.Ptr is the\ndeprecated spelling of reflect.Pointer, and render/validate.go''s sample\npage paths are now named, which is also what the fixture was demonstrating\n(the same path appears as both a BasePath and an Href within one entry).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQA1oiLcidYknHhwTGYK2qna8sAXtfJU8fukADlRnZH5wfFhu3OP4qi21ovmryQKc2r\nMa6Ge/xf0New7+x2C/igM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T16:05:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGU0MTk1M2E2MWMzZGJmYzAyN2JkNDZmMDkzZmEwOTJiZDg5MDljMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156","sha":"7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156"}],"sha":"e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/e41953a61c3dbfc027bd46f093fa092bd8909c28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:17:26Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:17:26Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"fix(auth): correct OIDCProvider''s issuer doc and rename roles -> scopes\n\nThree defects in one small struct, one of them live (#21).\n\n1. `oidcProviderURL` was documented as \"the well known URL\", but the\n   consumer hands the value straight to go-oidc''s NewProvider, which\n   appends `/.well-known/openid-configuration` itself and then requires\n   the issuer advertised there to equal what it was given. A CR author\n   following the doc fails twice over: measured against Google, the\n   doubled path 404s, and the issuer comparison rejects it independently.\n   The doc now says ISSUER, and a CEL rule rejects the discovery-document\n   suffix at admission so the mistake is caught where it is made rather\n   than as an unexplained auth subsystem that never builds. MaxLength is\n   there to keep the rule inside the apiserver''s cost budget -- an\n   unbounded field would make the WHOLE CRD fail to install.\n\n2. `Scopes` serialized as `roles` and was documented as roles, while the\n   consumer appends the values to the OAuth 2.0 scope list. An author\n   asking for a scope had to write it under a key named for something\n   else, and an author who wrote a role name there had it sent to the IdP\n   as a scope -- which most providers reject the entire authorization\n   request over. host-manager#190 turns this from a wart into a trap by\n   giving the field a real documented use (`offline_access`), so the key\n   is now `scopes` and the doc says what it does.\n\n3. The same field had no `omitempty`, so a nil slice marshalled to JSON\n   `null` against a `type: array` schema. nexus-manager''s mutating webhook\n   round-trips a KDexHost through these Go types, so the apiserver was\n   handed back -- and rejected -- an object into which nobody had written\n   the field: `spec.auth.oidcProvider.roles: Invalid value: \"null\"`. That\n   wedged the `public` tenant in SyncError and cost it a pinned workaround\n   in infra before the cause was found. Same class as #19.\n\nThe rename prunes rather than breaks: unknown fields on this CRD are\ndropped with a warning, verified by server dry-run against the live\ntenant, and tenant syncs are client-side apply. infra''s forced\n`roles: []` overlay becomes a no-op and can be deleted -- with omitempty\nthe null it worked around cannot occur.\n\nVerified: the regenerated CRD installs on a real apiserver (server-side\ndry-run), so the CEL rule compiles, type-checks and fits the cost budget.\n\nFixes #21\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"872c5b72e9c1b3c3af2d0cd04bbf2f2bff845cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/872c5b72e9c1b3c3af2d0cd04bbf2f2bff845cde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156","verification":{"payload":"tree 872c5b72e9c1b3c3af2d0cd04bbf2f2bff845cde\nparent 5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787930246 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787930246 -0400\n\nfix(auth): correct OIDCProvider''s issuer doc and rename roles -> scopes\n\nThree defects in one small struct, one of them live (#21).\n\n1. `oidcProviderURL` was documented as \"the well known URL\", but the\n   consumer hands the value straight to go-oidc''s NewProvider, which\n   appends `/.well-known/openid-configuration` itself and then requires\n   the issuer advertised there to equal what it was given. A CR author\n   following the doc fails twice over: measured against Google, the\n   doubled path 404s, and the issuer comparison rejects it independently.\n   The doc now says ISSUER, and a CEL rule rejects the discovery-document\n   suffix at admission so the mistake is caught where it is made rather\n   than as an unexplained auth subsystem that never builds. MaxLength is\n   there to keep the rule inside the apiserver''s cost budget -- an\n   unbounded field would make the WHOLE CRD fail to install.\n\n2. `Scopes` serialized as `roles` and was documented as roles, while the\n   consumer appends the values to the OAuth 2.0 scope list. An author\n   asking for a scope had to write it under a key named for something\n   else, and an author who wrote a role name there had it sent to the IdP\n   as a scope -- which most providers reject the entire authorization\n   request over. host-manager#190 turns this from a wart into a trap by\n   giving the field a real documented use (`offline_access`), so the key\n   is now `scopes` and the doc says what it does.\n\n3. The same field had no `omitempty`, so a nil slice marshalled to JSON\n   `null` against a `type: array` schema. nexus-manager''s mutating webhook\n   round-trips a KDexHost through these Go types, so the apiserver was\n   handed back -- and rejected -- an object into which nobody had written\n   the field: `spec.auth.oidcProvider.roles: Invalid value: \"null\"`. That\n   wedged the `public` tenant in SyncError and cost it a pinned workaround\n   in infra before the cause was found. Same class as #19.\n\nThe rename prunes rather than breaks: unknown fields on this CRD are\ndropped with a warning, verified by server dry-run against the live\ntenant, and tenant syncs are client-side apply. infra''s forced\n`roles: []` overlay becomes a no-op and can be deleted -- with omitempty\nthe null it worked around cannot occur.\n\nVerified: the regenerated CRD installs on a real apiserver (server-side\ndry-run), so the CEL rule compiles, type-checks and fits the cost budget.\n\nFixes #21\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLp8JjUDvfsNfnAXjWT08HPG0wlNdYu21Rl8bhUG/of4AgUuk1h91J/B4WBO2R4MKg\nCC86WqWHr4oRQIVuHAFwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T15:17:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKDdlMjdlZmI5NDY1MzEwMmVlOGQ5NTBlOGFkOWI5YTc2NGY3N2QxNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9","sha":"5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9"}],"sha":"7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/7e27efb94653102ee8d950e8ad9b9a764f77d156"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:31:01Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:31:01Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"fix(types): make optional struct fields pointers so omitempty applies (#19)\n\nencoding/json only honours omitempty for basic types, maps, slices, pointers\nand interfaces, so a value struct declared with omitempty was marshalled\nunconditionally. Every stored CR gained a key its author never wrote, and\nhas() on that field was unconditionally true in CEL, so no rule could test\nthe field''s own presence.\n\nThe issue listed five instances. A go/types scan of api/v1alpha1, corroborated\nby an independent reflection walk over every scheme-registered type, found\nseven -- both agreeing exactly:\n\n  Auth.JWT                    JWT\n  Metadata.Contact            ContactInfo\n  KDexFunctionSpec.Metadata   KDexFunctionMetadata\n  KDexFunctionSpec.Origin     FunctionOrigin\n  KDexHostSpec.Registries     Registries\n  NavigationHints.Weight      resource.Quantity          (not in the issue)\n  Runtime.Resources           corev1.ResourceRequirements (not in the issue)\n\nQuantity is a struct with a custom marshaller, so an unset navigation weight\ndid not surface as {} -- it surfaced as weight: \"0\", the other half of the\nArgo drift in knowdrive-site#116 that this issue was raised from. ObjectMeta,\nListMeta and Status match the pattern too, but those are Kubernetes API\nconvention rather than ours; TestNoOptionalValueStructFields records them as\nan allowlist and fails on anything new, so the class cannot silently regrow.\n\nThe generated CRD schema is byte-identical for all seven, as is\nCRD_REFERENCE.md -- verified by regenerating, not assumed -- so no CRD\nversion bump or stored-object migration is required.\n\nThe origin/backend mutex rule still had to change: with origin optional,\nhas(self.origin.executable) errors outright on an object that omits origin,\nso the rule needs a leading has(self.origin) guard. It does NOT get the\ncollapse to !(has(self.origin) && has(self.backend)) the issue proposed.\nEight KDexFunctions in dev -- every knowdb function plus proxy-chat -- are\nstored today with both a phantom origin: {} and a real backend, and the short\nform rejects every subsequent write to them, because a three-way merge never\nremoves a live key the manifest never mentioned. An envtest spec in\nnexus-manager pins all four cases and fails on exactly that one under the\ncollapsed rule. The code comment records the condition for collapsing it\nlater, once no cluster still stores an empty origin.\n\nA nil pointer selector compiles exactly as a value selector did, so the\ncompiler flags none of the reads this turns into panics. accessors.go gives\nreaders back the old semantics -- an unset field reads as an empty one --\nso call sites do not each have to remember.\n\nOne behaviour change: JWT is the only affected struct carrying\nkubebuilder:default markers, so a host with auth: {} no longer has\njwt.cookieName / jwt.tokenTTL materialized by the apiserver. host-manager\nalready falls back to those same values, so runtime behaviour is unchanged.\n\nCloses #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b1a1e06ca455ab651c4eb3ee118a3bd873fb55e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/4b1a1e06ca455ab651c4eb3ee118a3bd873fb55e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b1a1e06ca455ab651c4eb3ee118a3bd873fb55e\nparent a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787167861 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1787167861 -0400\n\nfix(types): make optional struct fields pointers so omitempty applies (#19)\n\nencoding/json only honours omitempty for basic types, maps, slices, pointers\nand interfaces, so a value struct declared with omitempty was marshalled\nunconditionally. Every stored CR gained a key its author never wrote, and\nhas() on that field was unconditionally true in CEL, so no rule could test\nthe field''s own presence.\n\nThe issue listed five instances. A go/types scan of api/v1alpha1, corroborated\nby an independent reflection walk over every scheme-registered type, found\nseven -- both agreeing exactly:\n\n  Auth.JWT                    JWT\n  Metadata.Contact            ContactInfo\n  KDexFunctionSpec.Metadata   KDexFunctionMetadata\n  KDexFunctionSpec.Origin     FunctionOrigin\n  KDexHostSpec.Registries     Registries\n  NavigationHints.Weight      resource.Quantity          (not in the issue)\n  Runtime.Resources           corev1.ResourceRequirements (not in the issue)\n\nQuantity is a struct with a custom marshaller, so an unset navigation weight\ndid not surface as {} -- it surfaced as weight: \"0\", the other half of the\nArgo drift in knowdrive-site#116 that this issue was raised from. ObjectMeta,\nListMeta and Status match the pattern too, but those are Kubernetes API\nconvention rather than ours; TestNoOptionalValueStructFields records them as\nan allowlist and fails on anything new, so the class cannot silently regrow.\n\nThe generated CRD schema is byte-identical for all seven, as is\nCRD_REFERENCE.md -- verified by regenerating, not assumed -- so no CRD\nversion bump or stored-object migration is required.\n\nThe origin/backend mutex rule still had to change: with origin optional,\nhas(self.origin.executable) errors outright on an object that omits origin,\nso the rule needs a leading has(self.origin) guard. It does NOT get the\ncollapse to !(has(self.origin) && has(self.backend)) the issue proposed.\nEight KDexFunctions in dev -- every knowdb function plus proxy-chat -- are\nstored today with both a phantom origin: {} and a real backend, and the short\nform rejects every subsequent write to them, because a three-way merge never\nremoves a live key the manifest never mentioned. An envtest spec in\nnexus-manager pins all four cases and fails on exactly that one under the\ncollapsed rule. The code comment records the condition for collapsing it\nlater, once no cluster still stores an empty origin.\n\nA nil pointer selector compiles exactly as a value selector did, so the\ncompiler flags none of the reads this turns into panics. accessors.go gives\nreaders back the old semantics -- an unset field reads as an empty one --\nso call sites do not each have to remember.\n\nOne behaviour change: JWT is the only affected struct carrying\nkubebuilder:default markers, so a host with auth: {} no longer has\njwt.cookieName / jwt.tokenTTL materialized by the apiserver. host-manager\nalready falls back to those same values, so runtime behaviour is unchanged.\n\nCloses #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIwP9L3aILdFNyjh3XWEpbHbvCmcclEV3lXyiUw9Si/6zJ77kTHOfdp8wH2fhaYS1K\n5Yxv10r8fKYuS4mPEyFQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:31:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKDVlMzBjMzQ5MmUwYTExYzFjOTNlYTdhODdlNDI1ZjgzZDcxY2VlZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b","sha":"a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b"}],"sha":"5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/5e30c3492e0a11c1c93ea7a87e425f83d71ceee9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:37:44Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T21:37:44Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"feat(function): raise API.Schemas maxProperties from 6 to 10\n\nSix named component schemas was the binding constraint on a KDexFunction''s\nOpenAPI contract, and it bound well before the others did: paths allows 16,\nand each path item carries up to 9 operations. A CRUD-shaped function spends\nthe budget on request/response pairs alone and has nothing left for the\nshared Error object and list envelope that make the document reusable,\nforcing authors to either inline schemas per operation (defeating $ref reuse)\nor split one logical API across several KDexFunction CRs (a schema-shaped\nconstraint driving a deployment-shaped decision).\n\nAPI is embedded only by KDexFunctionSpec, so kdexfunctions is the only CRD\naffected. Nothing else caps the count: nexus-manager''s webhook validator\nassembles the document for the vacuum linter and host-manager consumes\nGetSchemas(), neither imposing a cardinality limit -- the CRD bound was the\nwhole gate, so the marker is the whole change.\n\nRaising a bound on a x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields map raises the\nmaximum object the apiserver will accept, and the CEL cost estimator budgets\nover the entire schema, so a regression there would make the whole CRD fail\nto install -- invisible to round-trip decode tests. Verified offline by\nrunning the apiserver''s own ValidateCustomResourceDefinition (schema +\nCEL cost) over all 29 generated CRDs: 0 rejected. That check was itself\nverified by inflating the paths bound the API-level rule iterates, which\ncorrectly tripped both the per-rule and whole-schema cost budgets.\n\nCloses #18\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WcsPAt1Q2T9phkWgu5QCEM","tree":{"sha":"9c75f0e6cc5069c89cf6245d49bd6aa28c5b8413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/9c75f0e6cc5069c89cf6245d49bd6aa28c5b8413"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c75f0e6cc5069c89cf6245d49bd6aa28c5b8413\nparent 7d67abc80abc63287209154e6a8442e58420cfca\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1786484264 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1786484264 -0400\n\nfeat(function): raise API.Schemas maxProperties from 6 to 10\n\nSix named component schemas was the binding constraint on a KDexFunction''s\nOpenAPI contract, and it bound well before the others did: paths allows 16,\nand each path item carries up to 9 operations. A CRUD-shaped function spends\nthe budget on request/response pairs alone and has nothing left for the\nshared Error object and list envelope that make the document reusable,\nforcing authors to either inline schemas per operation (defeating $ref reuse)\nor split one logical API across several KDexFunction CRs (a schema-shaped\nconstraint driving a deployment-shaped decision).\n\nAPI is embedded only by KDexFunctionSpec, so kdexfunctions is the only CRD\naffected. Nothing else caps the count: nexus-manager''s webhook validator\nassembles the document for the vacuum linter and host-manager consumes\nGetSchemas(), neither imposing a cardinality limit -- the CRD bound was the\nwhole gate, so the marker is the whole change.\n\nRaising a bound on a x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields map raises the\nmaximum object the apiserver will accept, and the CEL cost estimator budgets\nover the entire schema, so a regression there would make the whole CRD fail\nto install -- invisible to round-trip decode tests. Verified offline by\nrunning the apiserver''s own ValidateCustomResourceDefinition (schema +\nCEL cost) over all 29 generated CRDs: 0 rejected. That check was itself\nverified by inflating the paths bound the API-level rule iterates, which\ncorrectly tripped both the per-rule and whole-schema cost budgets.\n\nCloses #18\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WcsPAt1Q2T9phkWgu5QCEM\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJ2TydJv+V84CgT4zFlmxHvT/bArekG6wajPEpvVoNK0HZlLxFBJg7QxGApPIL09i0\nttqU+dpyQ79MpaTKm7TQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T21:42:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGE4OTFmYzdlODdiOTM0ZGU4NzQwYWFmMDhmZjI4ZjkwMjFlOTY1M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/7d67abc80abc63287209154e6a8442e58420cfca","sha":"7d67abc80abc63287209154e6a8442e58420cfca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/7d67abc80abc63287209154e6a8442e58420cfca"}],"sha":"a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/a891fc7e87b934de8740aaf08ff28f9021e9653b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty30