":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/ca4dbd44243b2c43998d940f6fb785070da4beda","sha":"ca4dbd44243b2c43998d940f6fb785070da4beda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/ca4dbd44243b2c43998d940f6fb785070da4beda"}],"sha":"2632fbd72278f131aed7a0cf1bd86f8fca1172f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/2632fbd72278f131aed7a0cf1bd86f8fca1172f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/ca4dbd44243b2c43998d940f6fb785070da4beda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T22:59:52Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T22:59:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kdexrole): opaque capability grants via PolicyRule.scopes (#15) (#16)\n\n* docs(spec): opaque capability grants on KDexRole (PolicyRule.scopes)\n\nDesign for kdex-crds#15: give PolicyRule a first-class `scopes` field for\nopaque (colon-less) capability entitlements, immune to wildcard grants. Each\nrule becomes structured (resources+verbs) XOR opaque (scopes), enforced by\nrule-level CEL. Paired host-manager buildMappingTable emit branch lands\ntogether. Enumerate-per-role (no catch-all); no entitlements-library change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plan): implementation plan for KDexRole opaque capability grants\n\n4 tasks: kdex-crds schema (scopes field + relaxed structured fields + CEL),\nupdateCrdUsage propagation, host-manager buildMappingTable emit branch,\nhost-manager envtest CEL characterization. TDD per task.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: release nexus-manager too (serialization); updateCrdUsage -t -n\n\nAll actors that deserialize a KDexRole must carry PolicyRule.Scopes or they\nprune the field on round-trip. Add nexus-manager release (Task 5) + switch\npropagation to ./updateCrdUsage.sh -t -n (dependent go.mod bumps left for review).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(kdexrole): opaque capability grants via PolicyRule.scopes\n\nAdd PolicyRule.Scopes for colon-less opaque entitlements; relax\nresources/verbs to optional; rule-level CEL enforces structured-XOR-opaque\nand rejects a colon in a scope. Resolves kdex-crds#15 (grant side).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8be7350a9c776df77dc75074eb567bcdb3eeb7e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/8be7350a9c776df77dc75074eb567bcdb3eeb7e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/ca4dbd44243b2c43998d940f6fb785070da4beda","verification":{"payload":"tree 8be7350a9c776df77dc75074eb567bcdb3eeb7e7\nparent 4a39f08e338ef1292b26af73638f64dbc36ee24a\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1784415592 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784415592 -0400\n\nfeat(kdexrole): opaque capability grants via PolicyRule.scopes (#15) (#16)\n\n* docs(spec): opaque capability grants on KDexRole (PolicyRule.scopes)\n\nDesign for kdex-crds#15: give PolicyRule a first-class `scopes` field for\nopaque (colon-less) capability entitlements, immune to wildcard grants. Each\nrule becomes structured (resources+verbs) XOR opaque (scopes), enforced by\nrule-level CEL. Paired host-manager buildMappingTable emit branch lands\ntogether. Enumerate-per-role (no catch-all); no entitlements-library change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plan): implementation plan for KDexRole opaque capability grants\n\n4 tasks: kdex-crds schema (scopes field + relaxed structured fields + CEL),\nupdateCrdUsage propagation, host-manager buildMappingTable emit branch,\nhost-manager envtest CEL characterization. TDD per task.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: release nexus-manager too (serialization); updateCrdUsage -t -n\n\nAll actors that deserialize a KDexRole must carry PolicyRule.Scopes or they\nprune the field on round-trip. Add nexus-manager release (Task 5) + switch\npropagation to ./updateCrdUsage.sh -t -n (dependent go.mod bumps left for review).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(kdexrole): opaque capability grants via PolicyRule.scopes\n\nAdd PolicyRule.Scopes for colon-less opaque entitlements; relax\nresources/verbs to optional; rule-level CEL enforces structured-XOR-opaque\nand rejects a colon in a scope. Resolves kdex-crds#15 (grant side).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXAVoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4/IQAGhgvmKx7ozH7L03Equ7v/gK\nNz923zWsnzQlh86ZanTL8KcvE+Bw7EpwVq63QE6CkBTktlM+eV9uGCnV8tt9kzdP\n