rganizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/dcbf7180f4a3226dce045407f72f5a510bb90352/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-25T01:14:14Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-25T01:14:14Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"kdexfunction: regenerate manifests + deepcopy for Builder.Cache\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcefda2c42c11c888377fc952f965ae509cca87b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/dcefda2c42c11c888377fc952f965ae509cca87b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/dcbf7180f4a3226dce045407f72f5a510bb90352","verification":{"payload":"tree dcefda2c42c11c888377fc952f965ae509cca87b\nparent fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779671654 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779671654 -0400\n\nkdexfunction: regenerate manifests + deepcopy for Builder.Cache\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBVA3dSGOjWxcEVZ+ult0PHgL9ayFrfDW7tdqPp6Qp7YMpGR5PCIWhqi6RdGXYanqA\nSOwcY7u0rc0pufAoMQ9w0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-25T01:14:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/dcbf7180f4a3226dce045407f72f5a510bb90352","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGRjYmY3MTgwZjRhMzIyNmRjZTA0NTQwN2Y3MmY1YTUxMGJiOTAzNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294","sha":"fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294"}],"sha":"dcbf7180f4a3226dce045407f72f5a510bb90352","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/dcbf7180f4a3226dce045407f72f5a510bb90352"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-25T01:14:07Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-25T01:14:07Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"kdexfunction: add Builder.Cache field for kpack PVC sizing\n\nThe kpack mutating webhook defaults Image.spec.cache.volume.size to \"2G\"\nwhen absent, which is too small for typical Go/Rust dep trees: builds\nexhaust the cache, repeatedly re-pull base layers, and link/compile\npeaks blow past container memory. Operators have been growing the\nunderlying PVCs by hand to 10Gi+, but k8s forbids shrinking PVCs - so\nonce a cache is grown, host-manager''s next reconcile (which strips\ncache from the spec, letting the webhook re-default to 2G) loops\nforever on \"field can not be less than status.capacity\".\n\nAdding an explicit Cache field on Builder lets host-manager write the\nright size onto the Image so the webhook''s small default never wins.\nThe field is optional; host-manager uses 10Gi as its fallback when\nnil. Operators wanting a different default set it via the chart values\non the FaaSAdaptor''s builders[]; per-function override via the\nKDexFunction CR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df5972b1a602bc56f06afc56b26a72b520c95d76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/df5972b1a602bc56f06afc56b26a72b520c95d76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294","verification":{"payload":"tree df5972b1a602bc56f06afc56b26a72b520c95d76\nparent 82646610dca33217903b5100391059b2a984d062\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779671647 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779671647 -0400\n\nkdexfunction: add Builder.Cache field for kpack PVC sizing\n\nThe kpack mutating webhook defaults Image.spec.cache.volume.size to \"2G\"\nwhen absent, which is too small for typical Go/Rust dep trees: builds\nexhaust the cache, repeatedly re-pull base layers, and link/compile\npeaks blow past container memory. Operators have been growing the\nunderlying PVCs by hand to 10Gi+, but k8s forbids shrinking PVCs - so\nonce a cache is grown, host-manager''s next reconcile (which strips\ncache from the spec, letting the webhook re-default to 2G) loops\nforever on \"field can not be less than status.capacity\".\n\nAdding an explicit Cache field on Builder lets host-manager write the\nright size onto the Image so the webhook''s small default never wins.\nThe field is optional; host-manager uses 10Gi as its fallback when\nnil. Operators wanting a different default set it via the chart values\non the FaaSAdaptor''s builders[]; per-function override via the\nKDexFunction CR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDJT9p+Mvf39F0//3y5qIX2A8GEqoQaZ4GQjfH2qYHdWhSiMc4L231KfSR5t+/+yuv\nj61SLoPIsS0lhrr6dI8A0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-25T01:14:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGZkYzYwOGQ3ZThjYzlhYjhiNWYyZDlhNjUxM2E4ZGIwNjg0Y2YyOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/82646610dca33217903b5100391059b2a984d062","sha":"82646610dca33217903b5100391059b2a984d062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/82646610dca33217903b5100391059b2a984d062"}],"sha":"fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/fdc608d7e8cc9ab8b5f2d9a6513a8db0684cf294"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/82646610dca33217903b5100391059b2a984d062/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-24T18:04:24Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-24T18:04:24Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"kdexfunction: fix mutex CEL to check origin subfields\n\nThe old rule has(self.origin) was always true because Origin is a\nvalue-type field with json:\",omitempty\" — Go''s omitempty does not\nsuppress zero-value structs, so spec.origin: {} is always present\nin marshaled JSON. The new rule checks origin''s three pointer\nsubfields (executable, generator, source) — each properly honors\nomitempty — so Origin is treated as \"present\" only when at least\none variant is populated.","tree":{"sha":"d3abb968d26b10b49f9f55630c8df33cfb8c3707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/d3abb968d26b10b49f9f55630c8df33cfb8c3707"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/82646610dca33217903b5100391059b2a984d062","verification":{"payload":"tree d3abb968d26b10b49f9f55630c8df33cfb8c3707\nparent dd3706cc8470ebfbb5b76ea493d90117ad440b0b\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779645864 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779645864 -0400\n\nkdexfunction: fix mutex CEL to check origin subfields\n\nThe old rule has(self.origin) was always true because Origin is a\nvalue-type field with json:\",omitempty\" — Go''s omitempty does not\nsuppress zero-value 