{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/7ec7e7a26d4a076c5754cd6a2ac55e4e578fb134/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T19:49:06Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T19:49:06Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"auth: document http-lookup-auth secret-type + HTTP endpoint contract\n\nAdds a SecretSelector entry for the kdex.dev/secret-type=http-lookup-auth\nSecret used by host-manager''s new HTTPLookup auth.Lookup implementation,\nincluding the wire-level request/response contract (HMAC signature header\nformat, JSON body, success/failure shape with the next_step Stage-2-MFA\nreservation) and a sniffer-shaped curl example for generating a matching\nKDexFunction CR via DevMode.","tree":{"sha":"2e8ff86ecfb7036b50fb29f70bec9ddb22d5cce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/2e8ff86ecfb7036b50fb29f70bec9ddb22d5cce2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/7ec7e7a26d4a076c5754cd6a2ac55e4e578fb134","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e8ff86ecfb7036b50fb29f70bec9ddb22d5cce2\nparent fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779133746 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1779133746 -0400\n\nauth: document http-lookup-auth secret-type + HTTP endpoint contract\n\nAdds a SecretSelector entry for the kdex.dev/secret-type=http-lookup-auth\nSecret used by host-manager''s new HTTPLookup auth.Lookup implementation,\nincluding the wire-level request/response contract (HMAC signature header\nformat, JSON body, success/failure shape with the next_step Stage-2-MFA\nreservation) and a sniffer-shaped curl example for generating a matching\nKDexFunction CR via DevMode.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAAVbcUhxT+53Jl2fTxhMrLmAIjY5ryl5Fy8y2sLAsjB6Mjy1tUdnnv8+X0eBOaDAs\nwZ5F8F5Gs/EP+Av9jFhgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-18T19:52:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/7ec7e7a26d4a076c5754cd6a2ac55e4e578fb134","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKDdlYzdlN2EyNmQ0YTA3NmM1NzU0Y2Q2YTJhYzU1ZTRlNTc4ZmIxMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8","sha":"fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8"}],"sha":"7ec7e7a26d4a076c5754cd6a2ac55e4e578fb134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/7ec7e7a26d4a076c5754cd6a2ac55e4e578fb134"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T20:29:39Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T20:29:39Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"npm: fall back to tarball package.json when manifest is sparse\n\nGitLab''s npm registry returns a per-version manifest that omits\ntype/main/module/exports/browser - it carries only name, version,\ndist, and devDependencies. hasESModule then rejects valid ES-module\npackages with \"package does not contain an ES module\" even though\nthe tarball''s actual package.json declares them correctly.\n\nWhen the per-version object lacks every ESM signal hasESModule\nconsults AND dist.tarball is present, download the tarball, locate\nthe canonical package/package.json entry, decode it, and re-run\nhasESModule against that. Same authorization header as the manifest\nfetch. This matches what `npm install` itself does - it never trusts\nthe registry''s metadata view for the shape of the package it''s\nabout to install.\n\nTests cover the happy path, the case where the tarball *also* lacks\nESM markers (still rejected), the sparse-manifest-no-tarball case,\nand the tarball-fetch-error case (original error joined with the\nfetch error). Closes kdex-tech/kdex-crds#2.","tree":{"sha":"746997cc52ee314f270c824445602a0c3e7781c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/746997cc52ee314f270c824445602a0c3e7781c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 746997cc52ee314f270c824445602a0c3e7781c1\nparent d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1778963379 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1778963379 -0400\n\nnpm: fall back to tarball package.json when manifest is sparse\n\nGitLab''s npm registry returns a per-version manifest that omits\ntype/main/module/exports/browser - it carries only name, version,\ndist, and devDependencies. hasESModule then rejects valid ES-module\npackages with \"package does not contain an ES module\" even though\nthe tarball''s actual package.json declares them correctly.\n\nWhen the per-version object lacks every ESM signal hasESModule\nconsults AND dist.tarball is present, download the tarball, locate\nthe canonical package/package.json entry, decode it, and re-run\nhasESModule against that. Same authorization header as the manifest\nfetch. This matches what `npm install` itself does - it never trusts\nthe registry''s metadata view for the shape of the package it''s\nabout to install.\n\nTests cover the happy path, the case where the tarball *also* lacks\nESM markers (still rejected), the sparse-manifest-no-tarball case,\nand the tarball-fetch-error case (original error joined with the\nfetch error). Closes kdex-tech/kdex-crds#2.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQO3EjnMGOMjt/Sib9W9mNHcIw0jp6rVTJmWeFUgEErAAuFMQt56PwmZ4i4PhwRr4do\nKHFaIrUjdPwiFW7nM1ZQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-16T20:30:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGZkNDdlNDU1NjQxNjYwMDhkZDYwNDgxMjMxNzVjYzE1NTQ0YWQwYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a","sha":"d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a"}],"sha":"fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/fd47e45564166008dd6048123175cc15544ad0a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T19:01:24Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T19:04:00Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"npm: preserve URL path in Registry for sub-path registries\n\nRegistry stored only the DNS host. GetPackageInfo then built fetch\nURLs as <scheme>://<host>/<package>, collapsing the registry path\nand producing 403/404 against the registry root for any npm\nregistry served from a URL sub-path (GitLab, Verdaccio behind\nreverse proxies, JFrog, etc.).\n\nAdd Registry.Path, populate it from the parsed host argument and\n.npmrc entries, and have GetAddress emit scheme://host[/path].\nParseNpmrc now keys registries by host+path so distinct sub-path\nregistries on the same DNS host don''t share auth credentials, and\nnewRegistry''s lookup matches both fields exactly.\n\nAdds GetAddress, NewRegistry, ParseNpmrc, and ValidatePackage test\ncases covering sub-path hosts and same-host/different-path\nisolation. Closes kdex-tech/kdex-crds#1.","tree":{"sha":"a466e0fc500abb62864d3c3d104d7a28b3e65396","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/a466e0fc500abb62864d3c3d104d7a28b3e65396"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a","verification":{"payload":"tree a466e0fc500abb62864d3c3d104d7a28b3e65396\nparent d8ca1ce1052c7336d1c7a861780e729b14f1c893\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1778958084 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1778958240 -0400\n\nnpm: preserve URL path in Registry for sub-path registries\n\nRegistry stored only the DNS host. GetPackageInfo then built fetch\nURLs as <scheme>://<host>/<package>, collapsing the registry path\nand producing 403/404 against the registry root for any npm\nregistry served from a URL sub-path (GitLab, Verdaccio behind\nreverse proxies, JFrog, etc.).\n\nAdd Registry.Path, populate it from the parsed host argument and\n.npmrc entries, and have GetAddress emit scheme://host[/path].\nParseNpmrc now keys registries by host+path so distinct sub-path\nregistries on the same DNS host don''t share auth credentials, and\nnewRegistry''s lookup matches both fields exactly.\n\nAdds GetAddress, NewRegistry, ParseNpmrc, and ValidatePackage test\ncases covering sub-path hosts and same-host/different-path\nisolation. Closes kdex-tech/kdex-crds#1.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEavx6/rlE9/MP7+Yq/BTjMdTAAPROt3ZFYjdyAG4OzlkDZscf0/Pk2Vlg185cQGiQ\nPhCHhWKnk/JH3vr9ETrAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-16T19:04:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a","node_id":"C_kwDOPv1QHtoAKGQ5Yjg1ZjYzMjIzMzI3MWZiZmZlMTA5ODM3MjNlNDc3MmNhNzY1N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commit/d8ca1ce1052c7336d1c7a861780e729b14f1c893","sha":"d8ca1ce1052c7336d1c7a861780e729b14f1c893","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d8ca1ce1052c7336d1c7a861780e729b14f1c893"}],"sha":"d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d9b85f632233271fbffe10983723e4772ca7657a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rotty3000","id":146764,"login":"rotty3000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Njc2NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/commits/d8ca1ce1052c7336d1c7a861780e729b14f1c893/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T16:20:53Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T16:20:53Z","email":"rayauge@doublebite.com","name":"Raymond Augé"},"message":"default backend Deployment template now PSS-restricted compliant\n\nLoadConfiguration''s embedded default is the canonical source for\nhost-manager''s BackendDefault.Deployment template (the operator''s\nchart values just override individual leaf fields like serverImage).\nUntil now that default had no securityContext at any level and used\ncontainerPort 80, making host-manager-created backend Deployments\nfail PodSecurity \"restricted\" admission with four violations:\n\n  allowPrivilegeEscalation != false\n  unrestricted capabilities (container must drop ALL)\n  runAsNonRoot != true\n  seccompProfile missing\n\nUpdate the embedded YAML to include:\n\n- Pod-level securityContext: runAsNonRoot, runAsUser/Group/fsGroup=65532\n  (kubernetes-distroless convention), seccompProfile RuntimeDefault.\n- Container-level securityContext: allowPrivilegeEscalation=false,\n  readOnlyRootFilesystem=true, capabilities.drop=[ALL].\n- containerPort: 8080 (so the container can bind without\n  CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE, which is dropped under restricted).\n\nThe Service spec keeps port 80 / targetPort: server. The named port\n\"server\" still resolves through Kubernetes Service to the new\ncontainerPort 8080, so HTTPRoute / Ingress backendRefs that target\nport 80 continue working unchanged.\n\nRequires the backend-static image to actually be non-root and listen\non 8080 - shipped as kdex-tech/backend-static:0.1.6 (rebuilt from\nkdex-tech/backend-static@d13d830). The operator''s chart values.yaml\nin kdex-tech/nexus-manager needs a matching serverImage bump to\n:0.1.6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"657dc180e263ce248200caea34bfae8dc431d9e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/trees/657dc180e263ce248200caea34bfae8dc431d9e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kdex-tech/kdex-crds/git/commits/d8ca1ce1052c7336d1c7a861780e729b14f1c893","verification":{"payload":"tree 657dc180e263ce248200caea34bfae8dc431d9e9\nparent 6c934210a25c72a80db7bdb2a7224b6bf4df2c69\nauthor Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1778948453 -0400\ncommitter Raymond Augé <rayauge@doublebite.com> 1778948453 -0400\n\ndefault backend Deployment template now PSS-restricted compliant\n\nLoadConfiguration''s embedded default is the canonical source for\nhost-manager''s BackendDefault.Deployment template (the operator''s\nchart values just override individual leaf fields like serverImage).\nUntil now that default had no securityContext at any level and used\ncontainerPort 80, making host-manager-created backend Deployments\nfail PodSecurity \"restricted\" admission with four violations:\n\n  allowPrivilegeEscalation != false\n  unrestricted capabilities (container must drop ALL)\n  runAsNonRoot != true\n  seccompProfile missing\n\nUpdate the embedded YAML to include:\n\n- Pod-level securityContext: runAsNonRoot, runAsUser/Group/fsGroup=65532\n  (kubernetes-distroless convention), seccompProfile RuntimeDefault.\n- Container-level securityContext: allowPrivilegeEscalation=false,\n  readOnlyRootFilesystem=true, capabilities.drop=[ALL].\n- containerPort: 8080 (so the container can bind without\n  CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE, which is dropped under restricted).\n\nThe Service spec keeps port 80 / targetPort: server. The named port\n\"server\" still resolves through Kubernetes Service to the new\ncontainerPort 8080, so HTTPRoute / Ingress backendRefs that target\nport 80 continue working unchanged.\n\nRequires the backend-static image to actually be non-root and listen\non 8080 - shipped as kdex-tech/backend-static:0.1.6 (rebuilt from\nkdex-tech/backend-static@d13d830). The operator''s chart values.yaml\nin kdex-tech/nexus-manager needs a matching serverImage bump to\n:0.1.6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkz/IkshVam7RsEHOJqfJnmZzKW\n6nB7fLHKMU+FCwWhUAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDHU7oscd1kuZO9OqLyT4/hQD2+ngkoNxMPrwsjj4VlvMVFKLQJOLTVYkMmF5/k9os\nrXf6or5aw2N7B0EMAlUQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-16T16:41:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146764?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rotty3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rott